From 8c239794fde1002d4200b7f3fb64ef66632667e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KaiLiu12 <74182067+onetrickollie@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:48:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Support side buttons that arrive as a middle click

Some mice declare more button bits in their HID report descriptor than
they give button usages to. A Delux mouse's "Wireless Receiver"
(VID 0x248A, PID 0x8566) declares 5 button bits but only usages
Button 1-3, so macOS gives bits 4 and 5 the middle-button usage. Both
side buttons then reach the event tap as otherMouseDown with button
number 2, the same as a wheel click, and are never turned into swipes.

RawButtonMonitor parses each mouse's report descriptor and only opens
devices with unnamed button bits. It reads their raw input reports and
records presses of those bits. When a button-2 press arrives, the event
tap waits up to 20 ms for a matching raw press; if one arrives, it posts
the back/forward swipe and swallows the middle click and its release.
Real wheel clicks pass through unchanged, and mice with complete
descriptors are not affected.

Reading raw reports needs Input Monitoring and the device.usb and
device.bluetooth sandbox entitlements.

Known limitation: the presses are recognized and the middle clicks are
swallowed, but in testing on macOS 27.2.1 the posted swipe did not
navigate in Safari or Chrome. That still needs investigating.
